==Acquisition==
*This mod can be acquired by attaining the rank of '''Flawless''' under {{Faction|New Loka}}, or the rank of '''Exalted''' under the {{Faction|Red Veil}}, and spending {{sc|25,000}} to purchase.

==Notes==
*Upon casting an ability with an imbued element, grants a <u>'''200%'''</u> Elemental Damage buff of the imbued element to all of Lavos's weapons for {{Stat|Ability Duration|icon=only}}'''20''' seconds.
**No buff will be granted when casting an ability with no element infused, or when casting [[Helminth]] abilities.
**Only one elemental bonus can be active at a time. Casting another ability with a mixed element will replace it and refresh the duration. 
*Bonus Elemental Damage will be added parallel to the weapon’s Elemental Damage, meaning it will NOT combine with elements on the weapon.
**Damage bonus is additive to elemental damage bonuses like {{M|Heated Charge}}.
*Due to how status [[Status_Effect#DoT_Damage_Scaling|DoT damage]] is calculated, a Valence Formation buff for {{D|Heat}}, {{D|Electricity}}, {{D|Toxin}}, or {{D|Gas}} will also add '''200%''' DoT damage to all procs of that specific element.
**{{D|Blast}} damage is exempt, as its proc damage does not scale with elemental damage.
**The bonus is '''additive''' to elemental damage bonuses like {{M|Heated Charge}}, and '''multiplicative''' to [[Faction Damage Bonus|Faction Damage]] bonuses like {{M|Bane of Grineer}} and [[Status Damage]] bonuses like {{M|Rifle Elementalist}}.
**'''The 200% bonus DoT damage also applies to matching status procs from all of Lavos's abilities,''' including Helminth abilities. 
***For example, a heat Valence Formation buff will triple the DoT damage from his {{A|Catalyze}}, heat-imbued {{A|Ophidian Bite}}, subsumed {{A|Thermal Sunder}}, etc. Note that the initial ability damage will be unaffected, only the resulting DoT will be increased.
***Valence Formation buff is applied immediately on cast (before the ability finishes its animation), allowing the ability cast that grants the buff to also benefit from the bonus DoT damage (if applicable).
**As the damage of the {{D|Gas}} status effect does not scale with equipped Heat and Toxin mods, Valence formation is one of the few ways to increase its damage.
*Unlike most other buffs in the game, Valence Formation '''cannot''' be negated by nullifying bubble or enemy abilities, nor by jumping [[Out Of Bounds]].
*Valence Formation is a [[Universal Weapon Bonuses|Universal Weapon Bonus]], meaning it not only applies to weapons but also to certain "weapon coded" abilities. Of the subsumable abilities, Valence Formation can give its elemental damage and guaranteed proc to {{A|Airburst}} (direct hits), {{A|Breach Surge}}, {{A|Null Star}}, {{A|Pyrotechnics}}, and {{A|Shuriken}}.
*Valence Formation is one of the only buffs in the game that affects the AoE explosion of {{M|Vile Discharge}}, though it will only add the guaranteed status effect, not the elemental damage.
**However, the proc (except for {{D|Radiation}}) will affect Lavos if he is within range, unless he has Valence Block active to negate it.

==Tips==
*This allows Lavos to freely deal with enemy weaknesses such as removing armor with {{D|Corrosive}} while wielding a {{D|Viral}} based weapon, or dealing with shields by adding {{D|Magnetic}} damage.
*Shotguns are ideal weapons to utilize with this augment as each pellet will gain the boosted damage and proc the element on every hit. 
**Conversely, beam weapons may be less effective than expected as modding for multishot will not increase the number of hits.
*Allows you to trigger {{Arcane|Melee Influence}} on demand without needing to mod Electric on your melee weapon.
*Allows you to generate chain reactions with {{Arcane|Pax Seeker}}.
*Can damage the [[Profit-Taker Orb]]'s shields, allowing Lavos to adapt when she changes her elemental weaknesses.
*In some cases, it can be beneficial to use an unranked version of this mod so that the innate status effects on the weapon are more likely to happen, while the element from Valence Formation will still be guaranteed on hit.
*While Valence Formation does alter status weighting, the selected status is still applied in addition to normal status procs, effectively letting you "double up" by modding status normally then stacking Valence Formation on top.

==Bugs==
*Does not affect the tether mode of the thrown {{Weapon|Ferrox}} or {{Weapon|Tenet Ferrox}}

